Determining species diversity of riparian trees in Pune. Data gathered by several volunteers and is available on iNaturalist. 

Aids in understanding of effect of anthropological activities on riparian fauna.

Eg: Terminalia arjuna is a keystone riparian species, however its disappearance from most riverbanks in Pune suggests either anthropogenic activities removing old growth
resulting in replacement with fast-growing species like Pongamia pinnata. It is also possibly an indicator of poor groundwater replenishment/water pollution since Arjuna
requires year round water and is sensitive to contaminated/polluted water.

